"""Minimal smoke-test board.

This is NOT a real design. It exists so the toolchain -- `ato build`, the
kicad-cli wrappers in scripts/, and benchmarks/ -- has something in-repo to run
against. Replace it when actual circuit work starts.

Two test points bridged together. Deliberately no resistor, capacitor or any
other part with a value: those are resolved by atopile's part picker, which in
0.15.x requires `ato auth login` and a network round-trip. Keeping the fixture
pick-free is what lets `ato build` run offline and unauthenticated in CI.

TestPoint is also used rather than a connector because the standard library
ships no connector module, and pulling one from the package registry would
reintroduce that same network dependency.
"""

import TestPoint

module App:
    tp_a = new TestPoint
    tp_b = new TestPoint

    tp_a.contact ~ tp_b.contact
